diff --git a/docs/data-transfer/README.md b/docs/data-transfer/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..802aab3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/data-transfer/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# Account exports and imports
+
+Admins can request an account export in Account Settings. Each person can request
+an export of their accessible cards from their own profile. Both run as background
+jobs and send a private download link by email. Links expire 24 hours after archive
+completion; an expiry job purges the archive. Personal exports include published
+cards and the requester's drafts on accessible boards, never someone else's drafts.
+
+A signed-in identity can upload an account ZIP at `/account/imports/new` without
+selecting an account. Import creates a new account, with new internal IDs and a new
+account URL. Existing identities are matched by normalized email without changing
+their credentials or other memberships. The importer becomes owner and can access
+all restored boards. Source owners become admins. Existing accounts are unchanged.
+
+## Archive format (version 1)
+
+The archive is a ZIP64-compatible ZIP using stored (uncompressed) entries:
+
+- `manifest.json`: `format: "fizzy"`, `version: 1`, `kind: "account"` or `"cards"`,
+  and account metadata.
+- `<record type>/<source UUID>.json`: record attributes. Card JSON also contains
+  readable HTML descriptions and comments with their bodies.
+- `rich_texts/<UUID>.json`: canonical rich text for boards, cards, and comments.
+- `attachments/<UUID>.json`: attachment names and owning record/blob references.
+- `blobs/<UUID>.json`: original filenames, content types, byte sizes, checksums,
+  and portable attachment references.
+- `files/<UUID>`: original, unmodified file bytes. UUID paths avoid unsafe or
+  duplicate user-supplied filenames; the original name is in blob metadata.
+
+Account archives include users and settings, boards and columns, cards and comments,
+assignments, steps, tags/taggings, closures, goldness, postponements, access rules,
+reactions, watches, pins, entropy settings, events, mentions, activity markers,
+rich text, avatars, card images, and embedded files. Login credentials, sessions,
+API tokens, integration secrets/configuration, notification delivery state,
+search caches, and previous transfer archives are not transferred. Search and
+storage accounting are rebuilt; importing does not replay normal activity callbacks.
+
+Only account archives can be restored. IDs and references must resolve within the
+archive. Blob and mention signatures and attachment URLs are regenerated for the
+destination instance. CRC32 and original file checksums are checked. Duplicate
+entries, unsafe paths, unsupported formats, and incomplete references are rejected.
+No archive paths are extracted directly to the filesystem.
+
+## Operations
+
+Run database migrations and background workers, and configure outgoing email before
+using this feature. The standard Active Storage service is used for both uploads and
+exports. Disk exports use a temporary ZIP; S3 exports stream directly to multipart
+upload. Imports use seekable storage range reads and a temporary file per restored
+blob, not a second full local copy of the ZIP. File data is streamed in bounded chunks,
+including ZIP64 archives over 500 GB. Ensure enough temporary disk for the largest
+individual attachment (or the whole ZIP when exporting on Disk), and configure web
+server upload limits/timeouts for the account archives users will upload.
+
+For defensive parsing, each JSON entry is limited to 16 MiB and the ZIP directory to
+128 MiB. Files themselves have no application-imposed size cap. Compressed/repacked
+archives are not accepted; upload the original Fizzy export.
+
+Restore happens inside a database transaction. An error rolls back the destination
+account, memberships, content, search records, and storage records, and deletes newly
+uploaded destination files. The source upload is purged when processing finishes.
+The import audit record retains its status and a safe failure reason for the email.
+
+Run the focused regression suite with `script/test-data-transfer`.
